  "articlePanels": [
    {"kind":"lede","html":"<p>UK care home compliance is not one job. It is a stack of recurring checks a registered manager has to keep on top of at once: mock CQC or Care Inspectorate inspections, infection prevention and control, health and safety, medication storage, safeguarding, care plan reviews, the staff training and supervision matrix, food hygiene, and accident and RIDDOR reporting.</p><p><strong>Care home compliance software</strong> is what pulls those checks off paper and into one place, so evidence is captured on the day and the group can see every home at once. This page sets out what each area covers, how often it recurs, and how quickler runs it over WhatsApp with no app. It also states plainly what quickler is <em>not</em>.</p>"},
    {"kind":"takeaways","heading":"The short version","html":"<ul><li>A UK care home keeps mock inspections, IPC, H&S, medication storage, safeguarding, care plan reviews, a training matrix, food hygiene and accident/RIDDOR records on a recurring cycle. See our <a href=\"/pages/uk-compliance-inspection-frequency-guide.html\">UK compliance inspection frequency guide</a> for how often each recurs.</li><li>Quickler runs each area as a WhatsApp workflow. Staff answer by text, voice note or photo. No app, no login.</li><li>The group gets one dashboard across every home, with overdue actions and photo-backed evidence.</li><li>Quickler is <strong>not</strong> a care records, eMAR or clinical system. It is the audit and evidence layer that sits alongside one.</li><li>Under UK GDPR the home is the data controller and quickler is the processor, acting on your instructions.</li><li>Pricing is [[price:bundles]].</li></ul>"},
    {"kind":"default","eyebrow":"What has to be kept","heading":"The compliance a UK care home carries","html":"<p>These are the recurring areas most UK care homes structure their compliance around. Quickler runs each as its own workflow, so the evidence for each is captured on the day and dated.</p><ul><li><strong>Mock inspections.</strong> A dry run against the regulator's framework before the real visit. In England that is the CQC single assessment framework; in Scotland the Care Inspectorate self-evaluation. See the <a href=\"/pages/cqc-compliance-audit-checklist-uk.html\">CQC compliance audit checklist</a> and the <a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-self-evaluation-scotland.html\">Care Inspectorate self-evaluation for Scotland</a>.</li><li><strong>Infection prevention and control.</strong> Hand hygiene, PPE, cleaning standards and the environment against the code of practice. See the <a href=\"/pages/ipc-audit-care-home-uk.html\">IPC audit for care homes</a>.</li><li><strong>Health and safety.</strong> Falls, moving and handling, hoists, fire and legionella awareness across the premises. See the <a href=\"/pages/care-home-health-safety-audit-uk.html\">care home health and safety audit</a>.</li><li><strong>Medication storage.</strong> Fridge and room temperatures, controlled drugs storage, stock and expiry. See the <a href=\"/pages/medication-storage-audit-care-uk.html\">medication storage audit</a>.</li><li><strong>Safeguarding.</strong> A periodic review that referrals, records and staff awareness are where they should be. See the <a href=\"/pages/safeguarding-audit-care-home-uk.html\">safeguarding audit</a>.</li><li><strong>Care plan reviews.</strong> A structured check that plans are current, signed and reflect the resident's needs. See the <a href=\"/pages/care-plan-audit-review-uk.html\">care plan audit and review</a>.</li><li><strong>Training and supervision.</strong> A live matrix of who is trained, who is due, and who has had supervision. See the <a href=\"/pages/staff-training-supervision-matrix-care-uk.html\">staff training and supervision matrix</a>.</li><li><strong>Food hygiene.</strong> Kitchen checks against the Food Standards Agency approach. See the <a href=\"/pages/care-home-kitchen-food-hygiene-audit-uk.html\">care home kitchen and food hygiene audit</a>.</li><li><strong>Accidents and RIDDOR.</strong> Incident capture with photos and the RIDDOR reportability question. See the <a href=\"/pages/accident-incident-riddor-care-home-uk.html\">accident, incident and RIDDOR record</a>.</li></ul>"},
    {"kind":"default","eyebrow":"How often each recurs","heading":"The recurring cycle","html":"<p>The value of software here is not the single check. It is the recurring cadence, run reliably, with the evidence dated as it happens. Some areas are daily or weekly, such as medication fridge temperatures and kitchen checks. Some are monthly, such as the infection control walk and the health and safety audit. Some are quarterly or on a rolling review, such as care plans and safeguarding. Some are event-driven, such as an accident record or a RIDDOR report.</p><p>Quickler holds the schedule and prompts the right person at the right time. The <a href=\"/pages/care-home-compliance-checklist-monthly-uk.html\">monthly care home compliance checklist</a> sets out a typical month, and the <a href=\"/pages/uk-compliance-inspection-frequency-guide.html\">inspection frequency guide</a> covers how often the wider set recurs. Because every finished check is timestamped, the dated trail is the evidence a regulator wants to see.</p>"},
    {"kind":"default","eyebrow":"How it runs","heading":"A workflow per area, one dashboard for the group","html":"<p>Each area above is a workflow. The person doing the check receives the prompts in their own WhatsApp and replies by text, voice note or photo. There is nothing to install and no login. Voice notes are transcribed automatically, and a photo can be attached against any finding as timestamped evidence.</p><p>When a check is finished, quickler produces a shareable web report and a permanent record, with optional PDF and CSV export, and turns each issue into an action with an owner and a date. For a group, a regional quality lead sees every home's position on one dashboard, without chasing a manager for a spreadsheet. See <a href=\"/pages/care-home-audit-software-uk.html\">care home audit software</a> for the mechanics, and <a href=\"/pages/quickler-for-care-homes.html\">quickler for care homes</a> for the overview. Domiciliary and home care teams run the same way, from the <a href=\"/pages/domiciliary-care-audit-app-uk.html\">domiciliary care audit app</a>.</p>"},
    {"kind":"default","eyebrow":"The honest boundary","heading":"What quickler is not","html":"<p>This matters, so we state it on every care page. Quickler audits the environment, the premises and the process. It is <strong>not</strong> a care records system, it is <strong>not</strong> an eMAR, and it is <strong>not</strong> a clinical record of any resident. It does not hold care plans or medication administration rounds, and it does not perform statutory examinations such as the LOLER thorough examination or the fire and legionella risk assessments.</p><p>It sits alongside your care planning and eMAR system, which stays the single source of truth for anything clinical. Quickler is the audit and evidence layer around it. When we say quickler runs a medication storage check, we mean the storage conditions, temperatures and stock, not the administration of any drug to any resident. If that distinction matters for your group, <a href=\"/pages/help/index.html#contact-form-section\">ask us</a>.</p>"},
    {"kind":"default","eyebrow":"Data ownership","heading":"Who owns the data","html":"<p>You do. Under UK GDPR the care home is the data controller and quickler is your processor, acting only on your instructions. You decide what each workflow captures, and we would always encourage keeping identifiable resident detail to the minimum a check actually needs. Erasure is available on request to hello@quickler.co.</p><p>On pricing: [[price:bundles]]. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, so you can add every manager, care worker and bank worker across the group and pay only for who actually files something. Everything is unlimited on a paid account, so anyone who reads but never files adds nothing to the cost.</p>"},
    {"kind":"faq","heading":"Care home compliance, answered","html":"<h3>What compliance does a UK care home have to keep on top of?</h3><p>The recurring set is mock CQC or Care Inspectorate inspections, infection prevention and control, health and safety, medication storage, safeguarding, care plan reviews, the staff training and supervision matrix, food hygiene, and accident and RIDDOR reporting. Each recurs on its own cadence, from daily temperature checks to quarterly reviews and event-driven incident records.</p><h3>Is quickler a care records or eMAR system?</h3><p>No, and we are honest about that. Quickler is not a care records, eMAR or clinical system, and it does not replace one. It is the audit and evidence layer that captures your checks and inspections, so it sits alongside your care records system rather than replacing it.</p><h3>How does care home compliance software help across a group?</h3><p>It gives a regional quality lead one dashboard across every home, showing each home's compliance position, its overdue actions and its photo-backed evidence, without chasing managers for spreadsheets. Because every check is completed in WhatsApp and dated automatically, the group view is a by-product of the work rather than a separate reporting task.</p><h3>Does it satisfy CQC or the Care Inspectorate?</h3><p>Quickler gives you clean, dated, photo-backed evidence that your checks were done, which is what inspectors want to see. It does not award or guarantee any rating, and we make no compliance claim on your behalf. Whether your specific evidence satisfies a regulator is a judgement for you and your inspector.</p><h3>Who owns the data?</h3><p>You do. Under UK GDPR the care home is the data controller and quickler is your processor, acting on your instructions. You can ask us to erase records by emailing hello@quickler.co.</p><h3>What does it cost?</h3><p>Pricing is £20 per active user per month with a £20 monthly minimum, plus a free tier of 20 reports a month, extra dormant users always free. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, and dormant users are free. There is a free forever tier of 20 reports a month with up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock.</p>"}
